## Safety Rationale

### What the fix does

Remove three lines from `create_order` in `victim-service/app.py`:

| Line | Content removed |
|------|----------------|
| 90 | `# BUG 2: bulk discount applied at line level ...` (comment) |
| 93 | `# ... and then applied a SECOND time on the order subtotal. Revenue leak.` (comment) |
| 94 | `# Correct behaviour: apply the bulk discount exactly once.` (comment) |
| 95 | `subtotal = apply_bulk_discount(subtotal, total_quantity)` ← **only executable change** |

The sole functional change is the deletion of line 95. The three comment lines are
removed only because they exist solely to describe the bug that is being fixed; keeping
them would leave misleading comments in production code.

### Why exactly one line of logic is removed (not modified)

The two existing approaches — discount per line (line 91) vs. discount on the subtotal
(line 95) — are mathematically equivalent when applied in isolation, because:

```
sum(x_i × 0.90) == 0.90 × sum(x_i)
```

Either call alone produces the correct 10 % reduction. The RCA and the in-code comment
both confirm that the per-line call (line 91) was written first; the subtotal call
(line 95) is the redundant duplicate. Removing line 95 therefore:

1. Keeps the discount code path that was already present and tested.
2. Adds zero new logic — it is a pure deletion.
3. Leaves `apply_bulk_discount` itself completely untouched.

### Blast radius of the change

| Scenario | Before fix | After fix |
|----------|-----------|-----------|
| `total_quantity > 10` | 10 % discount applied twice → effective 19 % reduction | 10 % discount applied once → correct |
| `total_quantity == 10` | `apply_bulk_discount` returns `amount` unchanged on both calls → no compounding | identical — no discount applied |
| `total_quantity < 10` | `apply_bulk_discount` returns `amount` unchanged on both calls → no compounding | identical — no discount applied |
| `GET /orders/{id}` | unaffected (no call to `apply_bulk_discount`) | identical |
| `GET /health` | unaffected | identical |
| Tax calculation | computed on doubly-discounted subtotal | computed on correctly-discounted subtotal |

No other function in `app.py` calls `apply_bulk_discount`, and no other file in
the service imports it, so the change is entirely self-contained.

